  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rhino &amp; Tiger Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant will establish the scientific foundation needed for a comprehensive conservation strategy for tigers and their prey in the Central Terai Landscape (CTL) of India and then support preparation of that strategy. The Recipient will do this by: (1) continuing to assess the status of tiger and prey populations across a human disturbance gradient represented by Pilibhit Reserve Forest, Dudhwa National Park, Kishanpur Wildlife Sanctuary, Katerniaghat Wildlife Sanctuary and the Nandhour region using state-of-the art survey designs and mark-recapture statistical estimators; (2) recapturing individual tigers in order to determine inter-annual movement distances in areas surveyed with camera traps in Year 1 of the project; (3) estimating functional connectivity across the CTL (from Gola River to Katerniaghat Wildlife Sanctuary) in order to identify key corridors and movement barriers in the Haldwani Pilibhit -Kishanpur - Dudhwa - Katerniaghat Forest complex; and (4) synthesizing information from the above 3 objectives into a comprehensive tiger conservation strategy for the CTL.</narrative>
  </description>
